      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 507</b></color></size>

    <b>The Constitution of India</b>

    <size=74%>Adopted 26 November 1949; in force 26 January 1950

    <i>Hand-calligraphed and illuminated original</i>

    Parliament of India, New Delhi</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    The Constituent Assembly, chaired by Rajendra Prasad, with B. R. Ambedkar leading the drafting committee, debated the Constitution for nearly three years. The original copies were hand-written by Prem Behari Narain Raizada and illuminated by artists of Santiniketan under Nandalal Bose. Its Preamble promises justice, liberty, equality and fraternity.</size>'
