  m_text: In 1885 the Indian National Congress met for the first time in Bombay. Over the next six decades the struggle for freedom grew from petitions into mass movements led by Mahatma Gandhi, alongside revolutionaries, reformers and leaders from every region and community. Independence came on 15 August 1947, together with the painful partition of the subcontinent. On 26 January 1950 India became a sovereign democratic republic under its own Constitution.
